$entries = [
    ['2026-11-24', 'Email the customer from an appointment (owner, decision T35): Email in the calendar\'s details rolls down To, Subject (filled in: "Your appointment on Tue 24 Nov at 10:00") and Message. New POST business/api/appointments/{id}/email (appointments.manage, Config\\Forms notForms) and AppointmentService::email() (150 and 5,000 characters, refuses a customer without an email or who stopped emails, audited appointment.emailed). NotificationQueue::message() queues event message with new columns xs_booking_notification_queue.subject VARCHAR(200) NULL and body TEXT NULL (migration 2026-12-03-100000_AddMessageToBookingQueue, additive, run before the code copy); bookings:dispatch sends it in the standard customer booking email (Channels::email: the text as typed, the subject as heading, the details, change link, Reply-To the business, unsubscribe). Shown as "Message from you" under Messages and on the Sent page (BookingNotifications::label()).'],
    ['2026-11-24', 'Appointment details dialog tidied, Reschedule always offered (owner): the calendar\'s details dialog has a header with the status as a coloured pill, an action row (Reschedule, Customer, Call, WhatsApp; no mailto link, the email is shown as text), the when, where, email and phone in one card, the booking form answers in two columns, status and notes, messages and the reference last. Reschedule swaps in its own view (Back returns): now, With, Date, the next free times in two columns, or type a time, Move appointment. A pending or confirmed appointment whose time has passed can now be moved by the business (decision T34; AppointmentService::canMove(), can_move in GET business/api/appointments/{id}); others say why the button is off. Customers still move only upcoming bookings. No table or route change.'],
    ['2026-11-24', 'Remove logo (owner): a Remove logo button beside the current logo on /business/profile/photos and admin edit, deleting in place like a gallery photo (directory.js, data-logo-delete). New routes POST business/profile/logo-delete (Business\\Profile::deleteLogo, profile.edit) and POST admin/logo-delete/{id} (Admin::deleteLogo); both call HandlesListingUploads::removeLogo(), which empties logo_path, deletes the file unless another profile uses the same one, and recalculates the score. Like a photo delete it does not enforce "a logo or one photo"; the next save does. Config\\Forms knows the owner route; owner manual updated. No table change.'],
    ['2026-11-24', 'Profile header logo without a white box in dark mode (owner): .dark .profile-head > .avatar-logo is transparent, so the logo sits on the page; logos on discovery cards keep their white box in dark mode. No table or route change.'],
    ['2026-11-24', 'Practitioner and team cards on the profile (owner): the photo, name and role are the card\'s head row, and qualifications, registration, areas of focus, biography and Book run the full width under it, in line with the rest of the page, instead of indented beside the photo. CSS only (.team-member is a grid, .team-member-body display: contents); the name is 16px. No table or route change.'],
    ['2026-11-24', 'Profile section headings hold while read (owner, first for Dr Bhatta #392): in the main column every section heading (description and its cards, practitioners, services, features, tags, brands, reviews, venue, open positions and the rest) stays at the top of the screen while its section scrolls, and the next one takes over as a section ends. CSS position: sticky only, no script: one rule in directory.css on the heading that is a direct child of each main column panel (.panel-title, .branch-section-title, or the heading row: new .panel-head on Reviews, .logo-strip-head on Brands), under the site header (117px on a phone, 109px from md) and from lg under the sticky profile header (--profile-head-h), lined up with the Contact card title beside it, before and while scrolling. The right column is unchanged. No table or route change.'],
    ['2026-11-24', 'Profile header logo on the right (owner: a cleaner name and second title): the logo moved from left of the name to the top right, above the share icons (show.php renders the text first, then .avatar, then .share-row; .profile-head grid places them, .profile-head-text new). On a phone the text takes the full width and the share icons and logo share the row under it. No table or route change.'],
    ['2026-11-24', 'Profile header place line without the suburb (owner): "Durban, KwaZulu-Natal" under the name and second title (show.php $headTown, _profile_head_parts.php); the suburb stands in only when a profile has no city. The full address stays in the contact panel. No table change.'],
    ['2026-11-24', 'Second title on a profile (owner, for Dr Bhatta #392): an optional line under the practice or business name ("Specialist Orthopaedic Surgeon in Durban · Partner at BMR Orthopaedics"), free on every plan, nothing shown when blank. New column xs_directory_listings.headline VARCHAR(160) NULL (migration 2026-12-02-100000_AddHeadlineToListings, additive, run before the code copy), OWNER_EDITABLE, on the Details page of the shared form (signup, /business, admin edit). ListingText::headlineProblem() holds it to the name\'s rules (no links, phone numbers, emoji or symbols; the middle dot and bar allowed), ALL CAPS tidied, 160 characters (ListingText::HEADLINE_MAX); admin is held to the length only. Shown in the profile header under the name (_profile_head_parts.php, .profile-headline) and on the welcome pack cover and profile page. Not in discovery cards, JSON-LD or the score.'],
    ['2026-11-24', 'Welcome pack names the plan by the profile\'s site (owner: a co.za pack said Plus): Verified, with the seal, on co.za and Plus on .app, whatever the dates say. An admin preview of a Free or lapsed co.za profile said "Welcome to Plus", and an .app row with a verified_until date would have said Verified. The pack email\'s plan line follows the same rule. No table change.'],
    ['2026-11-24', 'A day or month click in the booking calendars no longer jumps (owner): on the public booking page a link that moves within its own step (a day, a month, Earlier, Later, Back) keeps the scroll where it is, only a time (to Your details) brings the next step into view; in the /business Book forms the week and month stay on screen, dimmed only when slow, while the next ones load, instead of shrinking to "Finding free times". No table or route change.'],
    ['2026-11-24', 'The /business Book forms in the public booking page\'s steps (owner): the calendar and availability dialogs and /business/appointments/new show Service as a list (length, price, where it is given: new FreeTimesBoard::servicePlaces()), With as buttons (only who offers the service; someone who does not is let go), each folded to one line with Change, then Choose a time: the month (book/_month.php in new button mode, data-cal-from and data-cal-month) above the week of free times, and Date and Time for any free minute. The selects stay the form\'s fields (hidden by free-times.js, with a Choose option when there is more than one); large step titles, Customer too. GET business/api/appointments/board takes ?month= and also returns calendar (FreeTimesBoard::month(), the business\'s rules, ten years ahead). Owner manual updated. No table or route change.'],
    ['2026-11-24', 'Public booking page step titles (owner): Service, With, Choose a time and Your details lose their numbers and are much larger (.book-step-title, text-2xl, sm:text-3xl). No table or route change.'],
    ['2026-11-24', 'Where each service is given, in the public booking page\'s service list (owner): under each service a map pin line per place (name only; the full address stays on the times and the summary), from PublicBookingService::placesFor() (the people who offer it and their working periods, T29; only the named person after a "Book with" link). Book::page passes servicePlaces while no service is chosen. No table or route change.'],
    ['2026-11-24', 'Choose a time by month on the public booking page (owner: better control, show the year): a month calendar (book/_month.php, "November 2026", Earlier and Later month, free days green, the week on view marked with the new avail-inview) sits beside the week of free times from xl, above it below (.book-pick). A free day opens its week (?from=); a month arrow opens that month\'s first free week (new ?month=, read by Book::page with PublicBookingService::month()). The week heading in book/_board.php now carries the year (both years when a week crosses New Year), also in the /business Book forms. No table or route change.'],
    ['2026-11-24', 'Booking steps without a page reload (owner: every date or time click flashed and jumped to the next section): on the public booking page and in "Change your booking", directory.js fetches the same page and swaps only the [data-book-steps] block (book/page.php #book-steps, book/manage.php #change), keeps the scroll, brings the next step into view smoothly only when it is off screen, and keeps Back and Forward working (history.pushState). It dims only when an answer is slow. Without script, or on any error or redirect, the plain links work as before. No table or route change.'],
    ['2026-11-23', 'Appointment summary on the public booking page (owner): beside the steps from lg (sticky), above them on a phone, filled on the server step by step: Service (length), Price (and the deposit, when asked), With, Date, Time (start to end), When (today, tomorrow, in N days) and Where (the chosen time\'s place with its address; one place is named from the start). One partial, book/_summary.php, now also draws the /business Book forms\' summary (empty rows that free-times.js fills). No table or route change.'],
    ['2026-11-23', 'Free times as one column per place (owner, decision T33): the place is no longer on each time but at the top of its column, a week at a time, only days with free times, Earlier and Later. New FreeTimesBoard (week(), places(), placesFor(); PublicBookingService::places() now delegates to it; AvailabilityService::providersFor() made public) and partial book/_board.php, used as links on the public booking page and as buttons in every /business Book form (calendar dialog, availability dialog, appointments/new). New GET business/api/appointments/board (appointments.manage, the member\'s scope; returns the board HTML); GET business/api/appointments/free and Appointments::freeNew() removed (the Move panel keeps GET {id}/free). The public page drops its Where step: Service, With, Choose a time (the board, ?from=), Your details; a picked time carries ?place=. Customers stop at the future limit, the business at ten years. No table change.'],
    ['2026-11-23', 'Free minutes after every booking now show on an empty day (owner: the setting seemed to do nothing): with "Times offered every: the service duration" (booking.slot_step 0) AvailabilityService::slots() spaces times by the whole booking, gap before + service + gap after + business.buffer_time, not the service length alone (a 60 minute service with 60 free minutes: 08:00, 10:00, 12:00). A fixed step (10, 15, 20, 30, 60) keeps its grid as before. The option reads "The service duration, with its free minutes". Applies to the public booking, the Book forms and the availability page alike. No table or route change.'],
    ['2026-11-23', 'Appointment summary on every Book form (owner): the calendar dialog, the availability dialog and /business/appointments/new show a card that fills in as the fields change: Service (with its length), With, Date, Time (start to end), When (today, tomorrow, in N days, in the business\'s time zone) and Where (the place the person\'s working hours give that time, from the free times already asked for; a time outside them says it is checked when you book). "Next free times" says the place once when every time shares it, so Where shows before a day is chosen. Service options carry data-name and data-duration. No table or route change.'],
    ['2026-11-23', 'One top bar for /business (owner): every page shows the same tools at the right of the top bar while the profile takes bookings, each for a member allowed to use it: Find (customers and appointments as you type, "/" opens it; new GET business/api/find in the customers.manage group, Customers::find(), scoped like the lists), Your booking page (new tab), Add a customer, Book an appointment (on a customer\'s page it books for that customer; on Calendar and Availability it opens their Book dialog in place). business/_topbar_tools.php, drawn by layouts/business.php into the new _shell section shell_tools; find.js; below lg the buttons are icons and Find opens over the bar. The copies they replace are gone: the dashboard\'s Book an appointment and Your booking page, the Customers page\'s Add a customer, the customer page\'s Book, the calendar\'s Book and Find. spa.js now starts page scripts in the swapped top bar too. New icons user-plus, calendar-plus. No table change.'],
    ['2026-11-23', 'Book from the availability page (owner: reception could not book from it, and the Book form was a narrow column to scroll): in the day view of /business/availability a free time opens a Book dialog on the page (resources/business/availability.js, same fields and JSON POST business/api/appointments as the calendar); after booking the page is fetched again in place (shell visit) and shows "Booked." with the reference. Without the script each time links to business/appointments/new filled in. A time several people share shows "Book with" and a link per person; AvailabilityOverview::day() times carry provider_ids. The shared Book fields (_appointment_fields.php, $wide) are two columns from lg up (when left, customer right) in the calendar dialog, this dialog and the plain page (no longer form-card-narrow); a chosen time folds the free times to one line with Change time; a day\'s times come in Morning, Afternoon, Evening rows showing only the time; the place is said once when every time shares it (dialog and availability page); the button reads "Book 09:20". Scope unchanged. No table or route change.'],
    ['2026-11-23', 'CSP lets GA4 with Google signals through: Config\\ContentSecurityPolicy::GOOGLE_SIGNALS (*.google.com, *.g.doubleclick.net, *.googletagmanager.com and the common Google country domains, google.co.za first) added to connect-src and img-src, as Google publishes for GA4. Production had logged about 1,600 blocked hits in November (www.google.co.za, stats.g.doubleclick.net, www.google.com/g/collect). A country domain cannot be wildcarded, so a visitor on an unlisted one still loses the signals hit. No table or route change.'],
    ['2026-11-23', 'Signed out shell pages get a brand bar and footer (owner: /business/sign-in and /admin/login looked bare): the top bar shows the WebScheduler Local logo linking to the site home and the theme switch (no menu button for a sidebar that is not there, no empty title), and a slim footer gives copyright, Privacy, Terms and Contact. layouts/business.php sets the bare section while signed out; _shell.php reads it and uses it up (admin.php reads the login page\'s and sets it again). Classes .shell-bare-brand, .shell-footer. No analytics added, no table or route change.'],
    ['2026-11-23', 'Owner user manual (owner): GET business/manual (Business\\Owner::manual, view business/manual.php), "User manual" under Plan in the /business sidebar for everyone signed in to a profile. Ten sections: getting started, the profile pages, messages from visitors (the Email this business relay: what the visitor sends, the email the owner gets, Reply goes straight to the visitor, limits, spam rules, POPIA), reviews (or "off" for medical and vets), jobs and service requests, stats, online bookings, Verified or Plus and the welcome pack, account and privacy, help. Worded per site, plan, profile kind and bookings; every limit read from the service that enforces it (ListingMessageService LIMIT_* and MAX_LINKS made public for this). "Print or save as PDF" ([data-print], delegated in directory.js) prints it as a document (.manual print rules in directory.css). New icons book-open and printer. No table change.'],
    ['2026-11-23', 'Welcome pack (owner): a branded PDF for Verified (co.za) and Plus (.app) profiles, emailed once when the plan first starts: cover and welcome letter, the profile ready to print with a QR code, an A4 QR poster, four counter cards to cut out, and a share kit (link, WhatsApp, email signature and social text, booking QR when bookings are on). WelcomePackService builds it from the live profile on every download (never stored), public facts only. New columns xs_directory_listings.welcome_pack_token (SHA-256 of the emailed link\'s token, unique) and welcome_pack_sent_at (migration 2026-12-01-100000_AddWelcomePackToListings, additive, run before the code copy). Routes GET welcome-pack/{token}, GET business/welcome-pack (card on the Plan page), GET admin/welcome-pack/{id} and POST admin/welcome-pack/{id}/send (panel on admin edit). New PHP dependencies dompdf/dompdf 3.1 and chillerlan/php-qrcode 5.0. .app packs carry the wordmark only (the badge logo says "in South Africa") and no Verified wording.'],
    ['2026-11-23', 'Profile editor on a bad connection (after the owner\'s save froze on #392 and the editor came up as raw HTML; production itself answered every save in under 0.25 s): a silent save now gives up after 25 seconds (AbortController in directory.js "silent save"), puts Save back and shows a red .save-toast.is-error that stays until clicked or the next save ("Not saved: the connection is too slow right now…"), and keeps the page and its edits; any other fetch failure still falls back to the plain post. When the rich text editor did not take over a field (rich-editor.js never arrived, or it failed to start), a .rt-missing notice above the plain box says why it shows formatting code and that reloading brings the editor back. No table or route change.'],
    ['2026-11-23', 'Communications shows the email footer (owner): the campaign form (new, draft, paused) and the Preview page show "Added under every email", the logo and company details every campaign email ends with (admin/communications/_footer_preview.php, class comms-footer-preview, no inline styles). Read only, from Config\\Company, whose new legalLines() and websiteLabel() word the footer once for the email and the admin view. No table or route change.'],
    ['2026-11-23', 'Email footer (owner): every customer email on emails/_layout.php (campaigns, verify, manage and preview links, booking emails, reminders) now ends with the WebScheduler Local logo and the company details under the card: WebScheduler (Pty) Ltd, registered in South Africa, registration number 2026/138798/07, +27 76 829 7070, za_admin@webscheduler.co.za, webscheduler.co.za. New Config\\Company holds the details and emails/_footer.php draws them; the logo is assets/brand/logo-64.png as an absolute URL. The same footer on both sites, because cron sends run as co.za. The holiday hours reminder, which copied the frame by hand, now extends the layout. Staff emails (admin-notify, verification-admin) unchanged. No table or route change.'],
    ['2026-11-23', 'Silent save in the profile editor (owner: every Save reloaded /business/profile and /admin/edit at the top). Save is sent in the background (directory.js "silent save", forms with data-silent-save) and answered with JSON by HandlesListingUploads::silentSave(): message (a .save-toast), new CSRF hash, updated_at for the unsaved draft copies, the strength panel redrawn; the success flash is taken back. Chosen files, team, branch or card rows added or removed, a new category, type or country, and the Where page (data-silent-save="reload", the pin may move) still reload, at the same scroll position; a rejected save reloads to show its messages as before. A plain post without the script is unchanged. No table or route change.'],
    ['2026-11-23', 'Bookings plan retired (owner, decision T32 in docs/bookings/decisions.md, supersedes T18 and T23): Bookings come with Verified on co.za and Plus on .app, and nothing else gates them. Removed Plans\\BookingPlanService, BookingPlanModel, Business\\PlanSettings and the Plan settings tab, emails/booking-plan.php, the bookings:plans command and its 04:40 cron line (cron reinstall needed at release), Config\\Bookings planRequired, planTiers, trialDays, planGraceDays and trialReminderDays, the routes business/settings/plan/subscribe, /cancel, business/plan/paystack and admin/bookings/{id}/extend, the business area trial banner, the API\'s plan_required error (OpenAPI file regenerated), SetupCheck plan_ended, the plan routing in PaystackPayments and the WSL-BKG-M reference prefix (retired, never reuse). bookings_in_premium() now follows bookings.enabled alone. /admin/bookings shows each business\'s paid plan (Verified or Plus) instead. No migration: xs_booking_plans and xs_booking_plan_payments stay, empty (both 0 rows on production, 23 Nov 2026), with no writer. Paystack held no Bookings plan.'],
    ['2026-11-23', 'Code audit cleanup (owner, 22 to 23 Nov 2026; no behaviour change for customers): removed the unused owner panel directory/_bookings_panel.php, six unused CSS classes, BookingAuthorization::hasRole() and TeamService::providerForMember(), and the four one off import commands (directory:import-doctors, -lenmed, -attorneys, -businesses; their signup_source values stay on the rows, and the Communications audiences still read them). Retired POST payfast/setup-notify (ProfileSetupNotify, ProfileSetupService::handleNotification(), PayFast::onceOffFields() and its CSRF, honeypot, bot trap and form health exemptions): profile setup is Paystack only, and the only PayFast orders on production were unpaid tests. Shared homes: Models\\Concerns\\HasStatusCounts (admin queue tab counts), Models\\Concerns\\ResolvesStoredPath (the one containment check for verification documents and careers CVs, pinned by ResolvesStoredPathTest), DirectoryListingModel::findPublishedBySlug(scoped: true) for the tap and discovery beacons, and Mailer::notice() now takes a reply to address, so careers and profile setup emails use it. The Bookings plan (bookings.planRequired) stays: it is built but not on sale.'],
    ['2026-11-22', 'Private uploads readable by the backup: VerificationDocumentProcessor (verification documents, careers CVs, menus) now stores files 0640 and creates folders 2770 (setgid, group www-data), not 0600 and 0700. The offsite backup runs as deploy, a member of www-data, and its tar failed on 22 Nov at 02:40 on a careers CV uploaded after the last release (the release chmod -R had hidden the fault until then; a new month folder would have failed the same way on 1 Dec). Nothing is world readable. Hotfixed on production 22 Nov (that file chmod 0640, backup rerun OK). No table or route change.'],
    ['2026-11-21', 'Communications (owner): /admin/communications sends a chosen email to a chosen group of profiles in daily batches. Templates in Config\\Campaigns (claim your practice profile, upgrade to Verified or Plus, announcement), each with editable subject and plain text paragraphs and merge fields ({name} {noun} {audience} {appearances} {site} {source}); audiences unclaimed imports, Free, Verified and Plus, narrowed by site, main category, province and signup source (CampaignAudience). A test send unlocks Start; Start snapshots the audience into the send log. New tables xs_campaigns and xs_campaign_recipients (unique campaign and profile) and columns xs_directory_listings.comms_opt_out_at / comms_opt_out_source (migration 2026-11-30-100000_CreateCampaigns, additive, run before the code copy). One opt out for all: the footer unsubscribe now stops the monthly report and every campaign, and opting back in from /business lifts both. New cron comms:send every 10 minutes 06:00 to 14:50 UTC (cron reinstall needed); a campaign pauses itself after 5 failed sends in a row. DirectoryListingMutationService::signInLink() is the shared 7 day sign in link (the profile nudge uses it too). No bulk send without the owner\'s OK, the POPIA basis and an SES quota check.'],
    ['2026-11-20', 'System watch (owner): /health gains a bookings check (dispatch and payments heartbeats in writable/watch/, due messages waiting over 15 minutes, failed messages in the last hour); new system:watch every 5 minutes emails the admin on health faults (hourly, on change, on recovery) and new CRITICAL/ERROR/ALERT/EMERGENCY log lines (each kind hourly), and --daily at 05:05 UTC sends a summary even when all is well; every cron line now runs through scripts/cron-job.sh, which records each job\'s end and emails when one fails; the cert expiry echo (lost to MAILTO="") moved into the summary. New writable dir watch/. Release copy is now cp -R --preserve=timestamps (cp -a reset writable/cache to 755 for seconds each release: 6 cache write errors). Cron reinstall needed.'],
    ['2026-11-20', 'Booking emails under load (dev only): php spark load:mail fire turns booking emails on for the load test practices (default rules, reminder 24 h before, owner and reception notices), books with load-flood.sh, runs the real NotificationDispatcher back to back under the bookings:dispatch lock, and checks every email sent against the database (own customer, team member of that practice, reception only for their people, practice/person/service and local time, the customer link key); then turns them off. First runs: 3,061 and 2,962 emails into Mailpit, 0 failed, all checks passed, no reminder sent twice. No production change.'],
    ['2026-11-20', 'Bookings under load (load test findings): CatalogueService and TeamService::saveHours() no longer delete a range (every link of a service, every period of a person), which took gap locks and deadlocked two businesses saving at once (12 at once: 30,491 of 37,195 saves failed before, 0 of 21,731 after); links change only where they differ, deleted by their full key, under a lock on the service or person row as BookingLock. New BookingMemo: settings, services and links read once per business per process (2 s at most; any write through those models forgets it), a booking went from 57 to 34 queries. The online booking now says why a time at the chosen place was refused (just booked, closed for a public holiday) instead of "Choose one of the times offered". Dev tools: load:race --trace|--saves|--flood, scripts/load-saves.sh and load-flood.sh. No table or route change.'],
    ['2026-11-20', 'Load test database (owner, dev only): commands load:db (copy the dev DB into webscheduler_loadtest through the app connection, keeping keys; load:db top lists the costliest queries from performance_schema), load:seed (500 Verified practices through the real booking services, deliberate wrong tries that must be refused, tallies in writable/loadtest/) and load:check (integrity and reception scope); npm run load:copy|on|off|status (scripts/dev-loaddb.sh). No production change, no new table.'],
    ['2026-11-19', 'Bookable person on the profile (owner, Dr Bhatta): the team card shows only "Book with {name}" (_team_booking.php); the person\'s week (times, places, services per period) and the Offers tags are gone from the card. PublicBookingService still builds week (weekLines()); the booking page is unchanged.'],
    ['2026-11-19', 'Team card on the profile (owner: cramped): each person\'s Qualifications, Professional registration, Areas of focus and Biography are their own part (.team-member-section) with a small heading and a hairline between; the registration line sits in a highlighted box. .panel h3 title rules now skip .team-member-section-title.'],
    ['2026-11-19', 'Team card form spacing (owner: cramped): in _person_fields.php (profile Team page, admin, Bookings person page) Qualifications, Areas of focus, Short bio and Photo are each a .person-section with a divider and room above, larger labels and a one line hint; Professional registration is a tinted panel (.team-registration) with a proper heading and an Optional chip.'],
    ['2026-11-19', 'Description cards (owner, for Dr Bhatta #392): the description (card 1, every plan) is capped at 3,000 plain characters again (RichText::MAX_PLAIN_LENGTH; text already over it still saves until edited), and Verified and Plus profiles can add up to 5 more cards on the Details page ("More about you"), each a heading and a rich text body of 3,000 characters, shown as their own panels after the description. New table xs_directory_listing_sections (migration 2026-11-29-100000_CreateDirectoryListingSections, additive, run before the code copy), written only by ListingSectionService (also called from syncChildRows(), so admin edit has them too). Discover finds a profile by its cards while its plan is live (DirectoryService::sectionExists(), filter only, never in relevance); the score ignores them. Free owners see one line pointing at the plan.'],
    ['2026-11-19', 'Health & Medical profile order (Config\\Verticals, owner): Practitioners (the team panel) now comes straight after "About my/our practice" instead of first; at a glance stays above the description.'],
    ['2026-11-19', 'Find a place by name (owner: a hospital\'s street is hard to work out, and the imported Netcare N17 Hospital address was in the wrong town): every address block on the profile forms (signup, owner Where and Branches, admin) has "At a hospital, medical centre or mall? Find it by name" above the address. Find (or Enter) sends one lookup to GET address-place (AddressSuggest::place, 10 a minute per IP), which asks OpenStreetMap\'s Nominatim (service(\'placeFinder\'), NominatimGeocoder::findPlaces(); always Nominatim, since Mapbox\'s geocoder has no named places; never per keystroke, as Nominatim\'s policy asks). Up to 5 named places in the form\'s country (roads, towns and areas left out, duplicates merged, cached 30 days); a pick fills street, suburb, city, province and postal code, puts an exact pin on the building, and names the location or branch when that is empty. Credit line "Place data © OpenStreetMap contributors". No new table or setting; privacy policies already name Nominatim.'],
    ['2026-11-18', 'Team card editors (owner): "Qualifications and credentials" and "Short bio" use the full description editor (paragraph style, bold, italic, underline, strike, lists, quote, link, align, spacing, indent), not the small one. Both are stored through RichText::sanitise, the description\'s allowlist (links get rel nofollow), and rendered with .listing-prose sized for a card. RichText::sanitiseBasic is removed; the caps (1000 and 1200 plain characters) are unchanged.'],
    ['2026-11-18', 'Team card short bio is rich text (owner): the same small editor as "Qualifications and credentials" (bold, italic, lists), stored through RichText::sanitiseBasic with the 1200 character cap counted in plain text (TeamMemberService::MAX_BIO_LENGTH, now public). xs_directory_listing_team.bio holds that HTML (column comment "plain text" is historic; old plain bios still render, as paragraphs); the profile renders it through sanitiseBasic, and the JSON-LD Person description is its plain text. The Bookings provider copy of the bio is shown only through the same path.'],
    ['2026-11-18', 'Rich text editor menus (owner): the description toolbar has a Paragraph style menu (Paragraph, Heading, Subheading, in place of the two heading buttons), an Align menu (in place of four buttons) and a Spacing menu: line spacing Single, Normal or Double, and space around paragraphs None, Normal or Large, per paragraph or heading. Stored as classes rt-lh-tight, rt-lh-double, rt-space-none, rt-space-large (RichText::CLASS_PATTERN; .listing-prose in directory.css draws them), so the CSP is unchanged; qualifications keep no classes.'],
    ['2026-11-18', 'Rich text editor (owner): Tiptap 3.34 replaces Quill 2.0.3 for the profile description and a person\'s qualifications. Built from resources/editor/rich-editor.js by npm run editor:build (vite.editor.config.mjs, now part of list:build) into public/assets/editor/rich-editor.js, self hosted and loaded only on the profile forms by directory/_editor_assets; public/assets/vendor/quill/ removed. New devDependencies @tiptap/core, @tiptap/pm, @tiptap/starter-kit, @tiptap/extensions. Own toolbar (headings, bold, italic, underline, strike, lists, quote, link row, alignment, indent, undo, redo, clear formatting; qualifications: bold, italic, lists, clear), no inline styles or injected CSS, so the CSP is unchanged. Alignment and indent stay the ql-align-* and ql-indent-* classes, so stored text opens unchanged. RichText now unwraps paragraphs inside a list item or quote (<li><p>x</p></li> becomes <li>x</li>).'],
    ['2026-11-18', 'Profile page on a desktop (owner): the breadcrumbs scroll away and the whole profile header (.profile-head-sticky in show.php) then stays under the site header while the gallery and content scroll beneath it; the right column (Contact first, then For patients, map, hours or branches, Open positions, as before) stays in view below the header and scrolls on its own when taller than the screen. directory.js measures the header into --profile-head-h. Phones and tablets unchanged.'],
    ['2026-11-18', 'Demo profiles (owner): the banner is neutral ("This is a demo profile", never "not a real business"), since a real practice\'s profile can be used as a demo (Dr Bertus Mensveld, #308, flagged is_demo by hand on production). A vacancy on a demo profile is labelled Demo on /jobs and its page, carries a notice, is noindex with no JobPosting JSON-LD, is left out of the sitemap, and Apply sends and stores nothing (JobBoardService::isDemo()).'],
    ['2026-11-18', 'Description heading per profile (Config\\Verticals, owner): Health & Medical reads "About {my} {noun}", filled by forCategory() from the profile type and its own noun: one doctor (type person) "About my practice", a group practice "About our practice", a hospital "About our hospital", a pharmacy "About our pharmacy". vertical_profile() and listing_vertical() pass the type.'],
    ['2026-11-18', 'Qualifications are a person\'s (owner): the profile wide Credentials box is gone from every form, the profile page and the JSON-LD business node; "Qualifications and credentials" on each team card is rich text (bold, italic, lists; RichText::sanitiseBasic, 1000 plain characters, a small Quill editor per person in directory.js, also on the Bookings person page). Team cards stay Verified/Plus only, so Free profiles show no qualifications (they can use the description). Health & Medical and the other groups that led with credentials now lead with the team panel. xs_directory_listing_team.credentials widened to TEXT (migration 2026-11-28-110000_WidenTeamCredentials, run before the code copy); new command directory:move-credentials [--apply] moves the old text onto the person card (one card: appended; an individual with none: a card is made), leaving practices with no person for review.'],
    ['2026-11-18', 'Profile section titles (resources/directory.css, owner): one style for every title on a profile, dark (no longer the category tint, and no longer small spaced capitals in the left column), normal case, bold: 24px in the left column (Qualifications & registrations, About my practice, Specialisations & treatments, Practitioners, Special interests...) and 18px on the right column cards (Contact, For patients, Rooms & practices, Map, Reception hours). The tint stays on the header and buttons.'],
    ['2026-11-18', 'Description styling (resources/directory.css): an owner\'s own headings in a profile description (.listing-prose h2, h3) are no longer caught by the panel title rules (small red capitals with wide letter spacing, which made them look like section titles); they are now Notion like, normal case and normal letter spacing, h2 18px and h3 15px semibold. The description editor (Quill, .rt-editor .ql-editor) uses the same rules, so it looks like the profile.'],
    ['2026-11-18', 'Health & Medical profiles (Config\\Verticals, owner): the description panel is headed "About my practice" (was "Business description") and services "Specialisations & treatments" (was "Treatments & fees"). Every other group unchanged.'],
    ['2026-11-18', 'Branch WhatsApp: xs_directory_practice_locations.whatsapp (migration 2026-11-28-100000_AddWhatsappToPracticeLocations, additive, run before the code copy). Each extra location can carry its own WhatsApp number on the Branches form (owner and admin), stored as wa.me digits by PracticeLocationService through whatsapp_digits() with the branch country\'s dialling code; its card on the profile shows its own Chat on WhatsApp button (greeting with the business name). A branch without one shows none, never the listing\'s number. First asked for by a practice with rooms at two hospitals (profile 392).'],
    ['2026-11-17', 'Mautic cleanup: removed NewsletterImportMautic command (newsletter:import-mautic) and NewsletterService::importFromMautic(); the import ran once (4 Nov 2026) and Mautic is retired. CONSENT_IMPORT constant kept because existing rows carry that value. marketing-site/ forms left for the Phase 5 old site cleanup.'],
    ['2026-11-17', 'Brand site (webscheduler-site, 7b63a90): medical first wording as on Local: header "Add your practice or business" ("Add profile" below 1280px), "free practice profile", "Discover local practices and businesses", platform line "for practices and businesses"; its terms, privacy, careers and partners pages unchanged. Released with npm run site:release.'],
    ['2026-11-17', 'Medical first, phase 4: Terms on co.za and .app dated 17 Nov 2026 (Legal::LAST_UPDATED, APP_LAST_UPDATED, so termsVersion() for new signups): "a local discovery and visibility platform for practices and businesses", "practice or business" in the not a party sentence, and Customer reviews says reviews are off on medical and veterinary profiles. PDFs rebuilt from their builders and published (profile guide, visibility playbook, Verified brochure, proposal): "free practice profile", "practice or business profile", and the guide\'s reviews page matches phase 3b; Config\\Documents profile guide summary to match. Brand site changes listed in docs/plans/2026-11-medical-focus.md for its own release.'],
    ['2026-11-17', 'Medical first, phase 3b: reviews are off and hidden on Health & Medical and Pets & Animals profiles until legal advice (Config\\Reviews::$offForGroups, ReviewService::offForGroup()). Nobody can write one whatever the owner switch says; the profile panel, result card and header stars and the JSON-LD aggregateRating and review show nothing, even for reviews already published; the owner panel says reviews are off for medical and veterinary profiles for now, with no switch; admin edit says so too. No data is deleted: taking a group off the list brings its reviews back. New helper listing_category_ref() (main category and slug from any row shape, shared with listing_vertical()).'],
    ['2026-11-17', 'Medical first, phase 3: the home page has a "Find a doctor, dentist or vet" row under the discovery box (DirectoryService::careEntryPoints(): the doctors set, dentist and veterinarian, each only while someone is published on that site, so it reads "Find a doctor or dentist" until a vet joins). Medical, vet and alternative medicine profiles get a "For patients" / "For clients" box under the contact card (_care_panel.php, listing_care_facts(), new Config\\Verticals key careFacts): the ticked features a patient asks about first, plus "Open in the evening" (a day closing after 18:00) and "Open on weekends" from the hours; those features leave "Features & amenities". The description helper writes health profiles in a new health family (Config\\DescriptionTemplates::$groupFamily). No change to discovery order, the header category strip (already medical) or Config\\Search (one vet category, "vet" already finds it).'],
    ['2026-11-17', 'Medical first wording, phase 2: owner copy names the profile\'s own place and its visitors from Config\\Verticals, through new keys ownerNoun ("practice" for health and vets, "pharmacy", "hospital", "organisation" for nonprofits and worship, else "business") and audience ("patients" for health, "clients" for vets and traditional medicine, else "customers"), read by listing_noun() and listing_audience() (directory_ui_helper, via listing_vertical(), which reads category_group, the nested category or a category_id lookup). Used in the verify, manage, preview, holiday hours, profile strength, Verified and Bookings plan and payment emails, the Verified panel, the reviews panel ("Reviews") and the preview bar. New category Medical Doctor (medical-doctor, Health & Medical, schema Physician with no medicalSpecialty) for doctors whose specialty is not known, and php spark directory:recategorise-imports [--report csv] [--apply] (dry run unless --apply) files uncategorised import-doctors and import-lenmed profiles titled Dr or Prof under it and lists the rest for admin. Release: run php spark db:seed DirectoryCategoriesSeeder, then the command as a dry run, and --apply only with the owner\'s OK.'],
    ['2026-11-17', 'Medical first wording, phase 1 (owner, 16 Nov 2026; docs/plans/2026-11-medical-focus.md): the header button says "Add your practice or business" ("Add profile" below 1280px), public pages and the signup form lead with practices ("Create your free practice profile", "Free Practice Profile", "Discover local practices and businesses"), the footer links say "Verified profiles" and "Plus profiles", and Config\\Directory::$siteDescription plus the .app copy (Config\\Sites::$appCopy) say the same; the home page heading has its own key, homeDiscoverTitle (it shared discoverTitle with the results page title, so .app showed the wrong one). Professional registers are South African only: each regulator in Config\\Registrations names its country and regulatorFor() takes the profile\'s (ProfessionalRegistration::countryOf()), so 347 doctor profiles in Botswana and Mozambique on .app are no longer offered an HPCSA box. Vets get the SAVC (South African Veterinary Council), co.za only. Home: the rotating strip says "Your practice." and the statement is "Behind every medical practice is a commitment to patient care." (owner, 17 Nov 2026). Code names and routes (/business, business_kind) are unchanged.'],
    ['2026-11-15', '.app countries: Mozambique, Eswatini, Lesotho, Zimbabwe and Zambia have full profiles in Config\\Countries (regions, timezone, dialling code, map box, currency). Mozambique had none, so /directory/mozambique, its region pages (Maputo City, Sofala) and its category pages answered 404 and were missing from the sitemap, although 274 imported profiles are there. Mozambique\'s province is "Maputo Province", so "Maputo" in Discover still means the city. No holiday calendars for the five yet.'],
    ['2026-11-14', 'Naming (owner): the South African upgrade is called "Verified", no longer "the Verified Business badge", across Local\'s pages, emails, flash messages, the Terms, the Privacy policy and the .app Terms (dated 14 Nov), the three PDFs and the brand site. Text about the picture itself (its use, copying and misuse in Terms section 20, .app Terms section 14 and /media) says "the Verified mark". Code names (routes such as business/badge, CSS classes, settings, PLAN_BADGE) and admin text are unchanged; new Paystack plans are named "WebScheduler Local Verified" (existing plans keep their names).'],
    ['2026-11-14', 'Brand site (webscheduler-site): standalone, self hosted Bookings is no longer sold. /pricing lost the Starter, Professional and Business plans and the international "ask for a price" box, the JSON-LD OfferCatalog and the /bookings SoftwareApplication lost their Bookings offers, facts.json lost bookingsStarter/Professional/Business, and the Bookings, home, about and FAQ pages say online bookings come with Verified and Plus. The brand privacy policy (dated 14 Nov) keeps section 4 for the businesses that already run the standalone app.'],
    ['2026-11-14', 'Documents: the profile guide and the business proposal (public/assets/documents/, built from marketing-site/outreach/) now say online bookings come with Verified, and carry the live prices (Verified R60 a month or R625 a year, profile setup R2 000; they still said R29.99 and R250) and the 5,000 character description limit. The proposal calls the .app upgrade Plus, not International Profile. The Verified brochure, whose source was lost, has a builder again (marketing-site/outreach/verified-brochure/, recreated from the published PDF with the same claims and sources), now with online bookings, the live prices and the plan called Verified.'],
    ['2026-11-13', 'Booking page: a Where step after the service (each place the service is given at, with its address and who works there; PublicBookingService::placesFor()), then With, times and the booking limited to that place (?place, AvailabilityService slots/availableDates/nextAvailable take a place). The day buttons became a month calendar of free days beside the chosen day\'s times, in two columns (book/_month.php, PublicBookingService::month()), the same calendar now on "Change your booking".'],
    ['2026-11-13', 'Brand site vhost (deploy/apache/webscheduler.co.za.conf, applied on the server 13 Nov 2026, backup /etc/apache2/webscheduler.co.za.conf.bak-20261113-slash): /x/ 301s to /x when x.html exists. /pricing/ and every other page with a trailing slash had answered 404 (five visitors to /pricing/ that day). Brand site also links the Fernwood demo profile and demo booking (webscheduler-site 1d65422).'],
    ['2026-11-13', 'Category matcher and Discover fixes (owner: new businesses could not find their category; "solar installation" found no solar business in the Discover dropdown). Profile forms (signup, owner Details, admin) ask "What does your business do?" and offer up to three categories (Search\\CategoryMatchService, Config\\CategoryMatch, GET add-profile/categories); a tap fills both selects. What was typed is kept with the category chosen (new tables xs_directory_category_matches, 180 days, purged by discovery:learn, and xs_directory_category_words); misses and Link are on /admin/discovery. Discover: a category read from the words also finds profiles outside it that use them, after its own (DirectoryService::applyCategory()); words match their stem ("installation" finds "installer", DiscoveryModelService::stem()); the dropdown offers the understood category first, the businesses that use every word, and "Discover every match" for everything typed. Migration 2026-11-27-100000_AddCategoryMatches.'],
    ['2026-11-12', 'Brand site: screenshots of the Fernwood Dental Studio demo (site/assets/screenshots/demo-*.webp, 1440 wide) on home (profile and bookings dashboard, replacing the PinkDrive profile and the standalone Bookings dashboard), Local (booking page) and Bookings (calendar Day view), each captioned or described as a demo practice.'],
    ['2026-11-12', 'Demo profiles: xs_directory_listings.is_demo (migration 2026-11-26-100000_AddIsDemoToListings), kept out of every discovery read by DirectoryService::published(); demo banner on the profile and booking pages (directory/_demo_banner.php), noindex, no structured data, Book::store() refuses. php spark demo:fernwood builds Fernwood Dental Studio, a fictional dental practice with a branch, four team members and six bookable services, for the brand site screenshots.'],
    ['2026-11-12', 'Brand site (webscheduler-site 5c68869): Local\'s look on every page (orange tracked eyebrows, .page-title, one accordion); online bookings come with Verified (South Africa) and Plus (every other country) on home, Local, Bookings, FAQ, Verified and pricing, "coming soon" removed; standalone Bookings plans stay, introduced as Bookings on its own infrastructure.'],
    ['2026-11-12', 'Terms (both sites): "What it includes" for the Verified Business badge (co.za section 4) and Plus (.app section 4) now lists online bookings; a lapsed badge or Plus stops new online bookings and keeps the calendar, appointments and customer records. Same day as the fraud terms, so Legal::LAST_UPDATED stays 2026-11-12.'],
    ['2026-11-12', 'Sales copy says online bookings come with Verified (co.za) and Plus (.app): home pricing cards and a new Your bookings moment, signup plan cards, /verified pitch, /plus page and owner Plus panel, FAQ on both sites (new #bookings question; the booking software answer now says they are one), the /compare booking row, the signup confirm email and the badge approved and activated emails, the Plus activated email. Every line checks bookings_in_premium() (directory_ui_helper: bookings on for the site and bookings.planRequired off, the BookingSetupService::whyNot() gate) and shares bookings_pitch(), so switching bookings off takes the promise down.'],
    ['2026-11-12', 'Bookings: customer names must be names (CustomerService::nameProblem(): letters in any script, spaces, apostrophes, hyphens, full stops, at least two letters, the contact person pattern ListingText::PERSON_ALLOWED) on the booking page, the Book dialog, the Customers form and the API; online the surname is always asked and required (no longer a Questions setting), the business side keeps it optional; after WSB-BOOK-000001 on production was booked as "dfhgfhfghj...45645645645". New answer types for the business\'s questions: A number, Letters and numbers (both with a shortest and longest length, booking.custom_field_N_min/max, 0 = any, up to 30) and South African ID number (co.za only, 13 digits with date of birth and check digit, never sent in a message).'],
    ['2026-11-12', 'Terms and privacy (both sites): false or fraudulent profiles and posts (terms co.za section 9, .app section 8, anchor #fraud; Jobs sections 6 and 5 point to it): unpublish at once, no refund, refuse new signups, keep the records as evidence, may report to the police (co.za: SAPS) and regulators on our own initiative; privacy policies allow that disclosure. Legal::LAST_UPDATED terms 2026-11-12.'],
    ['2026-11-12', 'The top bar is the page header (shell_title, shell_actions; no h1 in views), tab strips dock under it, the shell pager docks at the foot of the screen with Previous and Next fixed. Profile editor (owner and admin): every section is a pane on one page, switched in place by the tabs, the sidebar and the strength steps (directory.js profile panes); the draft backup keeps one draft per section form. The bookings Services and Team pages, when they are the profile\'s sections, carry the same docked tabs (App\\Services\\ProfileSectionTabs). Fixed: directory.js never loaded on /business/profile/* since 10 Nov (a view() with saveData false inside the page wiped the layout\'s profileForm flag; now a profile_form section).'],
    ['2026-11-12', 'One look for the app shell (owner): /admin and /business pages fill the width beside the sidebar like the calendar, with one page head (h1.page-title), one tab strip (.page-tabs), one box (.panel), two heading sizes, ocean Save and the three corner sizes (ShellStyleStandardTest). Profile editor: section tabs, one panel per section and a sticky Save and strength column from 1280px, a save bar below. Admin profile editor in the same tabs plus Admin (GET/POST /admin/edit/{id}/{tab}, Admin::editTabInput(): a tab posts only its own fields, the rest as stored); /admin/new stays one form. Every paged list uses the frontend pager (directory/_pager.php): /admin/profiles, the admin queues through pager_links() (reviews, jobs, verifications, referrals, partners, career applications, profile setup orders, now 50 a page instead of the first 200), the Jobs board, and the owner area through pager_result() (customers, notices, reviews, activity, sent messages, payments; notices and reviews used to stop at 50).'],
    ['2026-11-12', 'Email this business: profile email addresses are private by default (xs_directory_listings.email_public, owner switch under Details, 0 for every profile). Visitors write at GET/POST /directory/{slug}/message[?branch=id]; ListingMessageService relays it from WebScheduler Local with Reply-To the visitor and sends the visitor a receipt; up to 3 attachments (PDF, JPEG, PNG, .docx; 5 MB each, 10 MB together, under the production 12 MB request limit), checked by VerificationDocumentProcessor::check() and never stored; Mailer takes in memory attachments and clears them after each send. New table xs_directory_listing_messages (hashed log, 90 days, purged by directory:stats). Directory::email answers 404 unless email_public is on. Privacy policy (both sites) and FAQ updated. Migration 2026-11-25-100000_AddEmailRelay.'],
    ['2026-11-11', 'Doctor near me: "doctor(s)" is every kind of doctor, not GPs only (Config\\Search::$categorySets, a main category made of the categories SchemaTypes publishes as Physician, ?group=doctors, noindex); a near me radius that finds nothing shows the nearest instead and says so (Directory::index(), widenedFrom); MapboxGeocoder refuses a street match outside the suburb asked for (inAskedPlace(), 3 km from the suburb centre or 15 km from the city), after the 1,266 imported doctors were found never geocoded and a trial run put three in the wrong place.'],
    ['2026-11-11', 'SEO review (docs/audits/2026-11-seo-review.md): every page of a qualifying list is indexable under its own canonical with rel prev/next (seo_paged()); .app sitemap no longer lists South African venues; ?province/?city alone is noindex; 404 has no canonical; capitalised profile slugs 301; one Person node per individual (team card is an @id reference); JobPosting closing day in the business timezone, currency and country from the post, jobLocation always unless remote; ItemList on /jobs and /careers; hreflang on every page both sites share; og:site_name, og:locale; profile panel headings are h2; hours, prices and salaries read "08:00 to 17:00" (no en dashes); long cache headers for versioned assets and uploads in both vhosts.'],
    ['2026-11-11', 'Profile strength reweighted (ListingQualityService): place 25 to 14, reach 20 to 16, hours 7 to 5; specialisations 3 x 4, features 2 x 4, six photos; new line Who we speak to (5, a real contact person). A booking link that is the website or the website plus an #anchor earns nothing. Good and Excellent also need 3 services, 1 feature and 1 specialisation (label only). Contact person must be a person\'s name (ListingText::personNameProblem(), signup, owner edit, branches). Prompted by #3164 at 86.'],
    ['2026-11-10', 'Owner area, step 2: the profile form is pages of /business/profile/{section} (Config\\ProfileSections, DirectoryListingMutationService::updateOwnSection(), Business\\Profile); badge, jobs, reviews and stats are /business/{badge,jobs,reviews,stats} (Business\\Owner). /manage/edit and its views are gone; /manage addresses redirect, old posts 307.'],
    ['2026-11-10', 'One owner area at /business (was /bookings and /manage): every owner, Free included, is an xs_accounts row with an admin membership of their profiles (OwnerAccess; emailed sign in link to the profile\'s email, old /manage links still sign in). BusinessAuth has an owner level (profile pages) and the bookings level (locked page when bookings are not usable). /bookings/... GETs 301 and POSTs 307 to /business/... New permissions profile.edit, profile.billing, jobs.manage, reviews.reply (admins).'],
    ['2026-11-10', 'Bookings: one person, one record (T31). A provider is its own profile team card (xs_booking_providers.team_member_id unique, xs_directory_listing_team.show_on_profile); the profile form and the Bookings person page share directory/_person_fields.php; Bookings only for Verified or Plus profiles. Migration 2026-11-24-100000_UnifyTeamPeople.'],
    ['2026-11-10', 'Bookings: the team email is its own notice for staff (emails/booking-team.php: customer contact, maps links, Open the appointment, Reply to the customer); the customer email gains a heading, maps links, opening hours, Add to Google Calendar, Terms and Privacy.'],
    ['2026-11-10', 'Bookings: the Book form and dialog show the next free times (GET /bookings/api/appointments/free, shared with Move); a click fills the date and time.'],
    ['2026-11-10', 'Bookings: a person follows the profile\'s opening hours (live, xs_booking_providers.hours_mode = profile, read through ProviderWeek) or keeps own hours; hours_seen asks when the opening hours change under own hours.'],
    ['2026-11-07', 'App shell for /admin and /bookings: sidebar, top bar and page swaps without reloads (layouts/_shell.php, resources/shell/), ported from Bookings; admin leaves the public layout and its Popular categories strip.'],
    ['2026-11-07', 'System handbook added at /admin/documents/system; document library (Config\Documents) puts every published PDF in public/assets/documents/.'],
    ['2026-11-07', 'Offsite backups to S3 af-south-1 live (8aaab6e).'],
    ['2026-11-05', 'Bookings phases 0 to 10 and .app merged to main, dark behind bookings.enabled (caf5511).'],
    ['2026-11-04', 'Mautic retired: own newsletter list (xs_newsletter_subscribers), brand site form posts to Local.'],
    ['2026-11-03', 'Paystack for every new payment, WSL- references (1428ee4).'],
    ['2026-11-02', 'Yearly billing; /pricing.json feeds the brand site (9942955).'],
    ['2026-11-01', 'Admin dashboard, profile statistics, form health; brand site moved to its own repo.'],
    ['2026-10-25', 'local.webscheduler.app live for every country but South Africa (b60ae84).'],
];
